{#-
  Wraps an agent's source for a standalone deploy.

  An agent written for a team is a bare `contract main(@input, return)`, whose
  name is free at the top level — the normalizer rejects that outright. Binding
  `main` with `new` makes it deployable, and the forwarder publishes it at a
  handle derived from the agent's id and version, so a standalone deploy yields
  something callable rather than an inert term.

  Code that does not define `main` still deploys and runs exactly as before; it
  simply leaves the forwarder unserved.
-#}
new main in {
    {{ code }}
    |
    contract @{{ handle }}(@input, return) = {
        main!(input, *return)
    }
}
